# Clerk

> Clerk is user management for developers: sign-up, sign-in, and prebuilt UI components, multi-tenant organizations, enterprise SSO, subscription billing, and machine-to-machine auth, with SDKs for Next.js, React, and most web and mobile frameworks.

For AI agents and automation, use the tools and markdown surfaces below. Append `.md` to any `/docs`, `/articles`, `/blog`, `/changelog`, or `/glossary` URL to get the page as markdown.

## When to use Clerk

Use Clerk when an application needs sign-up, sign-in, and user management: prebuilt UI components, social login, MFA, multi-tenant organizations, enterprise SSO and SCIM, subscription billing, or machine-to-machine and API-key auth. Point a coding agent at the skill below or install the CLI; API specs are under API references.

## Agent setup

- [Clerk Skills](https://clerk.com/SKILL.md): One file that routes a coding agent to the right framework-specific skill
- [Clerk CLI](https://clerk.com/docs/cli.md): Commands, flags, and agent workflows. Install with `npm install -g clerk` or the [install script](https://clerk.com/install)
- [Clerk MCP server](https://mcp.clerk.com/mcp): Sign in once and let an agent read and configure your Clerk apps from an MCP client. Follow the [setup guide](https://clerk.com/docs/guides/ai/mcp/clerk-mcp-server.md)
- [Agent registration](https://clerk.com/auth.md): Provision an accountless Clerk application and keys without an account
- [Skills discovery](https://clerk.com/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json): Every individually published skill
- [Ship auth with AI agents](https://clerk.com/agents): How agent-driven Clerk setup works, end to end

